Ensure that you also run these tests under various different versions of the .NET Framework since different versions may behave differently. 

The ultimate goal of testing is to achieve a higher success rate in catching errors and unexpected behavior even before the application hits production stages. So, using automated testing tools and frameworks can significantly help in achieving this goal. Pex provides such an automated testing tool for .NET code with its Exploration-Guided Instrumentation capability.

Finally, keep in mind that the success of the testing process also heavily relies on the design and structure of the ArrayList class, and how you have implemented its methods. The more well-designed and implemented class and methods you have, the easier it will be to develop reliable tests for them. In this case, ArrayList class appears to be well-designed and implemented which in turn will provide a smoother testing process.
